{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-02-004", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": [], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Champions Young Olympians at Dakar 2026, First-Ever Olympic Event on African Continent", "content": "Samsung Electronics, a Worldwide Olympic and Paralympic Partner, today announced that it is bringing Galaxy technology and athlete-centered programming to the Youth Olympic Games Dakar 2026 to enrich the experience of young athletes during an important stage in their Olympic journeys. Taking place in Senegal from Oct. 31 to Nov. 13, Dakar 2026 is bringing […]", "sources": [{"name": "samsung_elec", "url": "https://news.samsung.com/global/samsung-champions-young-olympians-at-dakar-2026-first-ever-olympic-event-on-african-continent", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-02-005", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Li Auto to deliver some new Mega MPVs with LCD displays, due to a shortage of Samsung's 29-inch automotive OLED panels", "content": "<p>Chinese automaker Li Auto says that it is facing a shortage of the custom <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/li-auto-launches-2026-mega-home-mpv-29-6k-amoled-display\">29-inch 6K automotive OLED display used in its new-generation Mega MPV</a>, and will temporarily deliver some vehicles with LCD displays instead. Tang Jing, who heads Li Auto's product line, says that the company unexpectedly received notice of a temporary supply disruption, and that supply is not expected to recover until aroun", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/li-auto-deliver-some-new-mega-mpvs-lcd-displays-due-shortage-samsungs-29-inch", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-02-006", "date": "2026-11-02", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rumor: Samsung is developing a 17-inch foldable OLED device that folds down to 8 inches", "content": "<p>A new rumor suggests that <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-oled\">Samsung</a> is developing a large foldable OLED device that offers a 17-inch display when fully open and folds down to an 8-inch size. The project has reportedly moved past the early planning stage, and Samsung is said to be working on several versions and test devices. Samsung has not confirmed any of this, and the price and launch date are unknown - reports suggest it will not arrive before 2027.</p><a href=\"https://", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/rumor-samsung-developing-17-inch-foldable-oled-device-folds-down-8-inches", "type": "rss"}]}
